ShapeFix: the repair of intersecting wires of a face never ends where two
arcs of one circle in two wires meet end to end (mitcad#495).

The case: an invalid chamfer's result (before patch 0941), the bottom face
of a boss whose rim came in arcs spread over several wires, healed with
ShapeFix_Shape: FixIntersectingWires intersected an arc of one wire with
the next arc of the same circle in another wire, and the intersection of
the two circles gave a segment of no length at their common vertex. Both
ends of the segment lie at a vertex, so each edge was to be cut there
(CutEdge) and the same pair intersected again "with modified ranges"
(without counting a modification). CutEdge of an edge that is not same
parameter, whose p-curve is a trimmed curve, cut it only when the trimmed
curve is a line, but answered that it had cut it for any trimmed curve: the
arcs were never cut, the segment stayed, and the loop never ended (the
import of a design hung in the kernel).

CutEdge now answers that it cut an edge only where it did: a trimmed curve
that is not a line is left as it is and reported so, and a line whose cut
keeps its whole range is no cut either. FixIntersectingWires then goes on
to the next pair of edges.

Synthetic: a planar face of two wires, each an arc of the circle of radius
7.5 (from 0.5 to 1 and from 1 to 1.5 radians, and two other spans) closed
by a chord, the arcs' edges not same parameter with trimmed circles as
p-curves: FixIntersectingWires returns (nothing to fix); before, it never
returned. With same-parameter edges it returned before as well.

Upstream: new.
